additional_findings.claim:
Fence stripping runs before the whole text is tried as JSON. As a result, a fully valid raw-JSON analysis whose string values contain ``` is mis-parsed:
- one ``` gives an unclosed-fence truncation flag and a parse failure;
- two ``` give 'no JSON object found';
- in the P10 hostile case, it gives strategy=repaired, ok=True and final_answer='' (a fragment).
This fails closed (phase8 incomplete, label None). It is inherited from the pre-P1 parser and kept on purpose as a guard by tests/test_phase10_render.py:113. Recorded data has 0 occurrences.

